# Auto-generated by Next.js 16's own `next dev` when it detects an AI coding
# agent in the environment (see node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js,
# ensureAgentRulesForDev in app-info-log.js, and @vercel/detect-agent). Verified
# via source read during the 2026-08 pre-merge audit — legitimate first-party
# Next.js behavior, not a supply-chain or injection issue. Ignored because the
# content is static dev-tooling boilerplate with no bearing on this project and
# would otherwise show up as "changed" on every contributor's first `next dev`.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
